Don't watchdog-reset on SDUP timeout after resume RESTRT

Upstream sdram.c reset_with_timing() writes SD_CS = ...|RESTRT_SET at
the end and returns without waiting for SDUP; init_late/selftest is
the real "SDRAM up?" check.

vc4-suspend's sdram_exit_selfrefresh() adds a 200000-iter SDUP wait
after RESTRT, and on Free PiZZa's first HW test that timeout fires
and triggers a watchdog reset -- even though the resume path had
cleanly made it through DDR PLL re-lock, SDRAM clock un-gate, and
DPHY/APHY DLL locks. Empirical result: with this patch, after RESTRT
SD_CS reads 0x00214E43 (SDUP bit 15 remains clear) but sdram_mem_test
passes and ZQ calibration completes -- SDRAM is functional even
though the SDUP bit isn't asserting.

Fix by matching upstream's model: after RESTRT, udelay(2000), poll
SDUP with a very generous 2000000-iter timeout, but on timeout just
warn and continue. sdram_mem_test is the real functional gate.

Also lift the uart_print_hex extern declaration up to the top DBG
block so the resume warning can print SD_CS as diagnostic info
without tripping -Wimplicit-function-declaration.

Apply on top of pristine vc4-suspend src/ with
`git apply --ignore-whitespace` (works standalone or on 0006).

diff --git a/src/suspend.c b/src/suspend.c
--- a/src/suspend.c
+++ b/src/suspend.c
@@ -264,6 +264,7 @@
  * ========================================================================== */
 #ifndef NDEBUG
 extern int printf(const char *fmt, ...);
+extern void uart_print_hex(uint32_t val);
 #define DBG(msg) printf(msg)
 #else
 #define DBG(msg) ((void)0)
@@ -883,15 +884,17 @@ void sdram_exit_selfrefresh(const sdram_config_t *cfg) {
              & ~(SD_CS_STOP_SET | SD_CS_STBY_SET))
             | SD_CS_RESTRT_SET;
 
-    /* Wait for SDRAM UP */
-    for (timeout = 200000; timeout > 0; --timeout) {
+    /* Upstream reset_with_timing does RESTRT and returns without waiting for
+     * SDUP; init_late/selftest is the real functional check. Give the
+     * controller settling time, log status, let sdram_mem_test be the gate. */
+    udelay(2000);
+    for (timeout = 2000000; timeout > 0; --timeout) {
         if (SD_CS & SD_CS_SDUP_SET) break;
     }
     if (timeout == 0) {
-        DBG("[suspend] FATAL: SDRAM controller failed to come up!\n");
-        PM_WDOG = PM_PASSWORD | 10;
-        PM_RSTC = PM_PASSWORD | PM_RSTC_WRCFG_FULL_RESET;
-        for (;;) { /* wait for watchdog */ }
+        DBG("[suspend] WARNING: SDUP still clear after RESTRT (SD_CS=");
+        uart_print_hex(SD_CS);
+        DBG("); continuing to mem test\n");
     }
 
     /* JEDEC-required: MR restore + ZQ recalibration after self-refresh exit.
